From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:46:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] LvglDisplayEngineDxe: Delete the previous screen when a
 form is drawn

Every call of FormDisplay() builds the form on a new screen and a new
group, and only the last pair is deleted, at ExitDisplay(). The browser
calls FormDisplay() again after every change of a question, so a setup
session leaks a whole window (cards, tiles, dock) per interaction:
LVGL keeps a loaded screen until it is deleted.

Delete the previous screen and its group once the new ones are in place.
The group goes first, so that its objects are detached before the screen
is deleted and no focus moves around in the old form.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c b/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c
index c3e1964..ba24553 100644
--- a/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c
+++ b/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c
@@ -5401,6 +5401,8 @@ LvglRenderForm (
 {
   EFI_STATUS  Status;
   lv_obj_t    *ContentPanel;
+  lv_obj_t    *PrevScreen;
+  lv_group_t  *PrevGroup;
   extern BOOLEAN mTickSupport;
 
   ASSERT (FormData != NULL);
@@ -5431,6 +5433,13 @@ LvglRenderForm (
   //
   AptioChromeTeardown ();
 
+  //
+  // The screen and the group of the previous form go once the new ones are
+  // in place: LVGL keeps a loaded screen until it is deleted.
+  //
+  PrevScreen = mSession.Screen;
+  PrevGroup  = mSession.Group;
+
   //
   // Set up session state.
   //
@@ -5543,9 +5552,18 @@ LvglRenderForm (
   //
 
   //
-  // Load the screen.
+  // Load the screen, then delete the previous one and its group. The group
+  // first: it detaches its objects, so that deleting the screen moves no
+  // focus around.
   //
   lv_screen_load (mSession.Screen);
+  if (PrevGroup != NULL) {
+    lv_group_delete (PrevGroup);
+  }
+
+  if ((PrevScreen != NULL) && (PrevScreen != mSession.Screen)) {
+    lv_obj_delete (PrevScreen);
+  }
 
   //
   // Restore keyboard focus. Prefer the destination field after a nav-time
